      "writtenOn": "2020-07-15T01:09:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Bazel API is to make the depset have an order and then call ToList() on it.  I originally thought that was because the conversion to a list was a cast that couldn\u0027t take an order.  After looking at the implementation I see some optimizations that are possible due to the order being known ahead of time.  Even if I don\u0027t do those optimizations now, making a DepSet have any possible ordering might preclude them if they are needed later, and I don\u0027t see a use case for the same DepSet with different ordering, so I think I should switch to putting the order in the DepSet.",
      "revId": "8c342cc5cf770f0cc4b07c66ec70e4ee89c85844",
